WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:04.303
-We're hanging out
with Eddie Murphy.

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:06.806
-Questlove,
you were at the party

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.941
when Prince had on those skates
that lit up?

00:00:08.941 --> 00:00:10.376
Those glitter skates?
-Yes.

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:12.378
-Okay, yeah.
-Valentine's.

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:14.580
-He had on glitter --
We went to a party at --

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.615
Prince had
a roller-skating party.

00:00:16.615 --> 00:00:17.717
-I heard about this story.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.085
-It was like 2:00 or 3:00
in the morning.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:20.620
And we're at his house.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.054
And Prince goes, "Who wants
to go roller-skating?"

00:00:22.054 --> 00:00:23.523
It was like, "What?"

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.692
And we went to this roller rink
at like 3:00 in the morning.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.727
You know how
some sneakers they would have,

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.162
when you walked,
they would light up?

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:31.997
He had skates that when he
skated, they would light up.

00:00:31.997 --> 00:00:33.266
-So, it was a dark skating

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:35.367
and you see just see Prince
skating around.

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:37.804
No way.
Questlove, you were there, too?

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:41.941
-Yeah, it was just you, me,
Larry Graham, and --

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.043
-There was a couple of people
scattered around.

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:44.978
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:46.212
-That's bizarre.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:47.413
I mean, can you --

00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:49.182
-It was surreal.

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:52.618
-Can you tell the Prince story
about your chef?

00:00:52.618 --> 00:00:54.453
-Oh, well, I was -- We --

00:00:54.453 --> 00:00:59.091
Where I live now, Prince
stayed a couple of houses down.

00:00:59.091 --> 00:01:00.459
And he was --

00:01:00.459 --> 00:01:03.129
My chef was leaving at
like 2:00 in the morning once.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:06.332
And a car goes by, you know,
purple car and the music,

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:07.666
and he's like,
"Whoa, that's Prince."

00:01:07.666 --> 00:01:10.636
And a hubcap comes off,
and it just kind of fall --

00:01:10.636 --> 00:01:11.971
And the car keeps going.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.206
And he picks the hubcap up,

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:16.008
and it's got the Prince thing
on the hubcap.

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:19.078
And the car goes and makes
a big U-turn and comes back,

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:21.514
and Prince says,
"Can I have my hubcap back?"

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:24.150
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.020
I was like,
"What a great moment you had."

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.190
-No one else has that story.
That's awesome.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.258
I was going to go through
some of the Eddie Murphy

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.393
folklore stories that I've
heard, if you don't mind.

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:36.228
If you don't want to talk
about it, you don't have to,

00:01:36.228 --> 00:01:37.530
but I'll just name
a couple things.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.331
-No cheap shots, though.
-No, I would never.

00:01:39.331 --> 00:01:41.935
I would never do that.
-I'm just kidding.

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.703
-Here's one --
You and Jerry Seinfeld

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:45.838
started your stand-up careers
at the same week

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:47.206
at the same comedy club.

00:01:47.206 --> 00:01:49.341
-Oh, yeah, we started both
at the Comic Strip

00:01:49.341 --> 00:01:50.609
at the same time, yes.

00:01:50.609 --> 00:01:51.644
-You did?
-Yeah.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:53.913
-Wow. Who ran that?
Do you remember?

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:56.082
-Lucien. Lucien Hold.
-Yeah, Lucien Hold.

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:57.550
-Lucien Hold.
-I used to do that club.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.285
Yeah, I love Lucien.
-Lucien Hold.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:01.554
That name means
"the devil's grip."

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:03.155
-No, it does not.
That does not --

00:02:03.155 --> 00:02:05.057
That's not -- That's not true.
-But, no, if you take it.

00:02:05.057 --> 00:02:07.126
-Lucifer.
Yeah, Lucien Hold.

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:08.327
The devil's grip.

00:02:08.327 --> 00:02:10.095
-Yeah, that's what...
But he was not the devil.

00:02:10.095 --> 00:02:11.964
-He was one of the nicest guys.

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:14.266
-Nicest guy.
Got so many people started.

00:02:14.266 --> 00:02:16.269
-Yeah, he really did.

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:17.803
Dan Aykroyd and Harold Ramis

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:19.872
wanted you to be one of
the original Ghostbusters,

00:02:19.872 --> 00:02:21.440
but you turned it down.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.342
-Yes, but I did
"Beverly Hills --"

00:02:23.342 --> 00:02:24.710
'cause I did
"Beverly Hills Cop."

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:26.412
-Oh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.482
So, you made a good movie.

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:31.050
-It wasn't like I turned it down

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.819
inasmuch as I wasn't available

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:34.453
'cause I was doing
this other movie.

00:02:34.453 --> 00:02:38.090
The only movie I ever
turned down that was a --

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:41.427
that became a big hit was that
"Who Framed Roger Rabbit."

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:42.695
-You were going to be in that?

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.997
-Yeah, I was going to be
the Bob Hoskins dude.

00:02:44.997 --> 00:02:48.167
And I was like, "What?
Animation and people.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.769
That sounds like
bull[bleep] to me."

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.704
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:56.642
Now every time I see it,
I feel like an idiot.

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:59.812
-After "48 Hrs." came out,
Marlon Brando called

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.013
and asked to have dinner
with you.

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:04.016
-Yeah, yes.
Yeah, that was surreal, too.

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:06.519
-And you had dinner with him?
-Yeah, a few times.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:08.487
A few times --
I went to his house

00:03:08.487 --> 00:03:10.022
and had dinner at a hotel.

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:12.624
I had a --

00:03:12.624 --> 00:03:14.527
You know
the most surreal moment?

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.428
'Cause I had just done "48 Hrs."

00:03:16.428 --> 00:03:20.132
And Brando told me
his favorite scene in the movie,

00:03:20.132 --> 00:03:22.001
but he was acting to me.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:25.972
And he goes, "When you said,

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:30.576
'I'm you're worst
[bleep] nightmare.

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:33.746
I'm a [bleep] with a badge.

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.715
That means I've got permission

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:38.884
to kick your [bleep] ass
whenever.'"

00:03:38.884 --> 00:03:40.486
And I was like, "This [bleep]"

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:43.189
-[ Laughs ] Whoa!

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:45.391
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.493
That's what I'm like right now.

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:50.696
-I was like,
"Damn, Marlon Brando.

00:03:50.696 --> 00:03:53.966
I ain't do the [bleep]
like that, Marlon Brando.

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:56.002
You should have been
in '48 Hrs.'"

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:57.036
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.972
-Oh, my God.

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:05.944
You have -- You have one of
the world's biggest collections

00:04:05.944 --> 00:04:07.246
of Elvis memorabilia.

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:09.482
-Not anymore.
I used to when I was younger.

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:11.684
-Yeah, not anymore.
-Yeah, I got a little older.

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:13.152
You know, it was kind of like,

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.987
"Hey, man,
why I got this [bleep]"

00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:18.223
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.223 --> 00:04:20.426
That was much as --
I still love Elvis,

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.227
but he was much cooler
when I was younger.

00:04:22.227 --> 00:04:23.529
When I got older
and I kind of --

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.264
You start to see
the whole picture.

00:04:25.264 --> 00:04:28.167
It was like, "Hey, man,
take that [bleep] off the wall."

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.135
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.135 --> 00:04:32.238
I had that jumpsuit on my wall.

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:35.274
-Yeah, "Why am I doing that?"

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:37.276
-Sell all the jumpsuits, man.

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:39.778
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.778 --> 00:04:42.048
-Right before you landed "SNL,"

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:44.583
you were fired from your job
as a shoe salesman.

00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:46.952
-I wasn't fired.
I quit that job.

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:52.892
I had worked at Chandler's Shoes
at the mall out on Long Island.

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:55.461
[ Laughs ]
And I quit.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:56.895
-You quit?
-Yes, I quit.

00:04:56.895 --> 00:04:58.530
-Chandler's?
-Chandler's Shoes.

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:01.034
-Well, everyone at Chandler's
Shoes, you missed out.

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:02.401
And thank you for this gift,

00:05:02.401 --> 00:05:05.004
'cause Eddie Murphy is now
with us and we're so happy.

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:06.205
Eddie Murphy, everybody.

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:09.074
Watch Eddie's return
to "Saturday Night Live"

00:05:09.074 --> 00:05:10.743
tomorrow night.

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:13.645
And check out
"Dolemite Is My Name" right now,

00:05:13.645 --> 00:05:15.248
streaming right now on Netflix.

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:16.249
Do it right now.

